# Project design system (reference)

Applies to **every** user-facing surface in this repo (CRM, auth, admin, marketing, shared components, dialogs, tables, forms). Match the reference dashboard: white cards on a light canvas, **teal primary** accents, mint secondary accents, neutral gray text, rounded corners, subtle depth.

**Source of truth:** `app/globals.css` (`--crm-*`, `--ds-*`, `--primary`). Do not invent parallel palettes.

## Colors

| Role | Use |
|------|-----|
| Canvas / page bg | `--crm-canvas` (`#f8f9fa`) or `ds-gray-50` |
| Nav / sidebar chrome | `--crm-sidebar-bg` (`#eef1f4`) |
| Primary accent | `--crm-accent`, `--primary`, `ds-primary-500` (`#0d9488`) |
| Emphasis / dark teal | `ds-primary-600` (`#0f766e`) |
| Secondary tint | `ds-primary-300` (`#2dd4bf`) |
| Cards | `bg-white`, shadcn `Card` |
| Text | headings `ds-gray-800`–`900`, body `ds-gray-600`–`700`, labels `ds-gray-400`–`500` |
| Borders / grid | `ds-gray-100`–`200` |

- No new primary accent hues (blue, purple, brand-orange) unless the user explicitly requests them.
- Success / warning / error: `ds-success-*`, `ds-warning-*`, `ds-error-*` only for semantic meaning.
- Prefer `ds-*` Tailwind classes and CSS variables over raw hex in TSX/CSS.

## Surfaces, type, icons

- Cards: white, `rounded-xl`, light border (`ds-gray-200` / `border-slate-200`), `shadow-sm`, padding `p-4`–`p-6`.
- Active nav / selected tab / highlighted KPI: `bg-ds-primary-500` or `bg-(--crm-accent)` + **white** text/icons; inactive = gray on light background.
- Titles and metrics: semibold/bold; labels: smaller + `text-ds-gray-500`.
- Icons: minimal line style; active = white on teal, inactive = gray.

## Charts and data viz

**Default: teal light shades only** — bars, areas, pie/donut segments, and heatmap cells use the light end of the primary scale unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.

| Use | Token / value |
|-----|----------------|
| Default bar/segment fill | `ds-primary-200` (`#5eead4`) or `ds-primary-300` (`#2dd4bf`) |
| Lighter fill / background band | `ds-primary-100`, `ds-primary-50`, or `rgba(13, 148, 136, 0.12)` |
| Multi-series (same chart) | Step through **light teal only**: `ds-primary-100` → `200` → `300` → `400` — never blue, purple, orange, or library defaults |
| Line / emphasis stroke | `ds-primary-500`–`600` on top of light fills |
| Comparison / muted series | `ds-gray-400`–`500` — not a second hue |
| Axes, grid, legend text | `ds-gray-100`–`200` grid; `ds-gray-400`–`500` labels |

- **Do not** use Recharts/Chart.js/theme rainbow palettes, `#8884d8`, `#82ca9d`, or semantic greens/oranges for generic charts (reserve `ds-success-*` / `ds-warning-*` only when the metric is explicitly success/warning).
- Reuse or extend `DASHBOARD_CHART` in `app/crm/dashboard/dashboard-theme.ts` (`barLight`, `salesFill`, etc.) — add new chart constants there instead of inline hex in components.
- Area fills: low-opacity teal/mint only; no saturated multi-color stacks.

## Actions

- Primary button: teal fill, white text, `rounded-lg`.
- Secondary: white surface + teal text/border; avoid gray-filled primaries.

## Checklist

1. Tokens from `globals.css` — not one-off hex.
2. Same visual language on mobile/tablet (see `responsive-ui-ux` rule).
